It is Sunday afternoon and I am at home.
In Mexico it is only morning.
I open my laptop and call my sister Sofia.
She answers immediately with a big smile on the screen.
"How did your first shift at the cafe go?" she asks.
I laugh and tell her about the chaos yesterday.
"The first coffee went totally wrong," I say.
"The milk ran all over the counter!"
"But the second one turned out really good."
Sofia drinks her own coffee in front of the camera.
"Did you understand the espresso machine?" she asks curiously.
"I tried it yesterday," I answer.
"Elif showed me everything in detail."
I explain to Sofia how good it all feels.
In my normal job I just sit at the laptop.
Now I am learning to do something completely new.
I am working with my hands, far away from tech.
"That sounds really wonderful, Maya," my sister says.
We speak for another hour about our week.
I really feel at home in Berlin now.
